 Member 3 (Endocrinologist): Assesses hormonal levels (including FSH, testosterone, and estradiol) to understand the patient's endocrine function and its impact on fertility.

Group 2 -  Diagnostic Evaluation Team (DET)  
 Member 1 (Andrologist (Lead)): Provides specialized care for male reproductive health, focusing on diagnosing and managing infertility and performing additional diagnostics such as semen analysis and hormonal studies.
 Member 2 (Reproductive Endocrinologist): Focuses on the role of hormones in male fertility and can guide on treatment options based on the hormonal imbalance findings.
 Member 3 (Radiologist): Conducts imaging studies (such as ultrasound) to assess the anatomical aspects of the reproductive system, looking for possible abnormalities that could affect fertility.

Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)  
 Member 1 (Senior Urologist (Lead)): Provides overarching expertise and consensus on the findings from the IAT and DET, and advises on further management options based on surgical perspectives if needed.
 Member 2 (Clinical Geneticist): Determines the implications of the found cytogenetic abnormality on the patient's fertility and can discuss the potential genetic counseling for the patient and his partner.
 Member 3 (Clinical Psychologist): Assesses the psychological impact of infertility on the patient and provides support and strategies for coping with stress and emotional challenges throughout the treatment process.


